var FT={"Blaster Master":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS24","d":"Weapons with the GC:VSS-F property add bonus damage on matching dice. You ignore GC:VSS-C. Make a ranged attack as a Bonus Action after Dash or Disengage.","full":"Raise Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Blaster Roulette.** When two of the damage dice you roll for a weapon with the GC:VSS-F property show the same number, you deal bonus damage equal to that number. Once per turn.\n**Ignore Cooldown.** You ignore the GC:VSS-C property of weapons.\n**Run and Gun.** When you take the Dash or Disengage action, you can make a ranged attack with a weapon as a Bonus Action.","pre":"Level 4+, Dex 13+","asi":["DEX"]},"Familiar Keeper":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS24","d":"Find Familiar always prepared, once per Long Rest free. Extra familiar forms. Reaction: give an attack by a creature near your familiar Disadvantage, Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Find Familiar.** You always have Find Familiar prepared. You can cast it as a Magic action with no slot and no Material components. That ability is the one you raised. After you cast it this way, finish a Long Rest to do so again.\n**Expanded Options.** Besides the normal forms, your familiar can be an Imp, a Pseudodragon, a Quasit, a Sphinx of Wonder or a Sprite.\n**Familiar Distraction.** When a creature within 5 feet of your familiar makes an attack roll, you can use your Reaction to give that roll Disadvantage. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Flex Caster":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS24","d":"Raise a spell's level by 1 with an extra slot. Recycle excess slot energy to regain a level 1 slot.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Upcast.** When you cast a spell that gets stronger with a higher-level slot (such as Magic Missile), you can spend one more slot to raise its effective level by 1, up to level 9.\n**Downcast.** When you cast a spell with a higher-level slot, you can recycle the extra energy instead of improving the spell. The spell is cast at its base level and you regain one expended level 1 slot.","pre":"Level 4+, Spellcasting","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Magitechnician":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS24","d":"Your magic items use a better save DC if higher. On a Short Rest recharge one item as if dawn had come, once per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Magic Item Expert.** If a magic item of yours calls for a saving throw, it uses this DC when higher: 8 plus the modifier of the ability you raised with this feat plus your Proficiency Bonus.\n**Magic Item Recharge.** When you finish a Short Rest, you can make one magic item that regains charges or properties recharge as if the next dawn had come. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Metabolistic Magic":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS24","d":"After failing a D20 Test, spend a spell slot to add 2 plus its level. On a Short Rest spend Hit Dice to regain slots, once per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Arcane Skill.** When you fail a D20 Test, you can spend a spell slot to add a bonus to the roll, which can turn it into a success. The bonus is 2 plus the level of the slot.\n**Vital Fuel.** When you finish a Short Rest, you can spend Hit Point Dice up to your Proficiency Bonus to regain spell slots. Choose slots whose combined level is no more than the number of Hit Dice spent. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.","pre":"Level 4+, Spellcasting","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Pyromaniac":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS24","d":"Fire Bolt. Burning Hands and Scorching Ray prepared, each free once per Long Rest. Reroll max Fire damage dice up to your Proficiency Bonus.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Firestarter Magic.** You know Fire Bolt and always have Burning Hands and Scorching Ray prepared. You can cast each of those two spells once without a slot, and need a Long Rest to do so again. You can also cast them with slots. The spellcasting ability is the one you raised.\n**Flare Damage.** When you deal Fire damage and roll the highest number on a damage die, you can roll that die again and add it, and keep rolling while you get the highest number. You can add at most a number of dice equal to your Proficiency Bonus (minimum 1).","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Shock Trooper":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS24","d":"When you roll Initiative without Disadvantage, draw a weapon and attack. Your Speed doubles in the first round of combat.","full":"Raise Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**First Strike.** When you roll Initiative and do not have Disadvantage on the roll, you can draw a weapon and make an attack with it.\n**Rapid Advance.** In the first round of each combat, your Speed is doubled.","pre":"Level 4+, Str or Dex 13+","asi":["STR","DEX"],"fx":{"notes":[["Note","Shock Trooper: first combat round Speed is doubled. On Initiative you can draw a weapon and attack"]]}},"Showman":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS24","d":"Performance proficiency (Expertise if you already have it). Bonus Action taunt: Disadvantage on a creature's next attack against others. Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Expert Performer.** You gain proficiency in Performance. If you already have it, you gain Expertise in it instead.\n**Taunt.** As a Bonus Action you can mock a creature within 15 feet. If it can hear you (it need not understand), it has Disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes against a creature other than you before the end of its next turn. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.","pre":"Level 4+, Cha 13+","asi":["CHA"],"fx":{"skills":["Performance"]}},"Spellblade":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS24","d":"Learn two blade cantrips. Swap an attack for one of them. Add a mental ability modifier to weapon attack rolls, Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Blade Cantrips.** You learn two of these cantrips: Arc Blade, Burning Blade, Frigid Blade or True Strike. The spellcasting ability is the one you raised. When you gain a character level you can change your picks.\n**Arcane Strike.** When you take the Attack action, you can replace one attack with a cast of Arc Blade, Burning Blade, Frigid Blade or True Strike.\n**Channeled Attack.** When you attack with a weapon you are proficient with using Strength or Dexterity, you can add your Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma modifier (minimum +1) to the attack roll. Choose the ability each time. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.","pre":"Level 4+, Int, Wis or Cha 13+","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]}};
